window.products.push({"id":674957,"name":"3pcs Kitchen Aid Pasta Roller, Fettuccine Spaghetti Cutter Attachment Stainless Pasta Roller Cutter Maker Stand Mixer Attachment Set","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71UK6BmWa4L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Remark:This pasta roller and cutters attachment is designed for KitchenAid Stand Mixers,but not a KitchenAid brand, KitchenAid is registered trademarks of their respective owners and are not endorsing, sponsoring  or associated with us . Scope of application: making Italian pasta and noodles Attachment Speed Noodle width Suggested Uses PASTA ROLLER 1 Up to 140mm See roller settings chart FETTUCCINE CUTTER 4 6.5mm Egg noddles Fettuccine SPAGHETTI CUTTER 4 2mm Spaghetti Thin fettuccine Linguine fini BEFORE FIRST USE To avoid damage, do not wash or immerse the attachment in water or other liquid. Do not wash in dishwasher.  Note: These attachment are designed for making pasta dough only. Do not cut or roll anything other than pasta to avoid damaging your pasta roller. CLEANING AND MAINTENANCE WARNING! Before cleaning, please ensure that the Switch knob is at the “OFF” position and the plug has been disconnected from the socket,otherwise it may cause an electric shock or injury risk. Never clean the pasta roller and cutters attachment when it is assembled in the stand mixer. It could result in an seriously injured. △ATTENTION! Do not use metal objects to clean out the pasta roller and cutters. Do not wash the attachment in the dishwasher, or immerse in water or other liquids. The attachment must be hand washed. △Note: * After cutting pasta, let the roller and cutters air dry for one hour, then remove and dried dough using the cleaning brush. If dried dough is difficult to remove, try tapping the attachment with your hand. Use a toothpick if necessary. * After cleaning out all remaining dried dough, polish the pasta roller and cutters with a soft, dry cloth and store in a dry place at room temperature. * To maintain properly we recommend using a light mineral oil to lubricate the gears. Add a drop of the mineral oil to each of the four corners of the pasta roller and cutters. IMPORTANT SAFEGUARDS When using electrical appliances and this attachment, basic safety precautions should always be followed, including the following: 1.Read all instructions. 2.This appliance is not intended for use by persons (including children) with reduce physical, sensory or mental capabilities, or lack of experience and knowledge, unless they have been given supervision or instruction concerning use of the appliance by a person responsible for their safety. 3.To avoid electric shocks, do not use this device in the vicinity of water. Do not immerse the stand mixer in water or other liquid. 4.Switch off the appliance and always disconnect the plug from the power socket (pull out the plug)  after each use of the appliance and the attachment, before assembling the attachment and accessories, changing accessories, cleaning or in case of malfunction. 5.Do not use stand mixer and t attachment without supervision. Always turn the appliance off, when you leave the room. Pull the plug cut of the socket. Close supervision is necessary when any appliance is used near children. 6.Keep the attachment away from children. The device should be used and stored out of the reach of children. 7.Avoid contacting moving parts, Keep fingers out of discharge opening. 8.Please place the appliance on a stable and flat table. It will cause injury if it is placed on uneven level. 9.Keep hands, utensils or other objects away from the pasta roller and cutters, or moving parts while it is in operation. 10.Do not touch any moving parts during the use. 11.Do not use the appliance if it is damaged. 12.Do not let the power cord fall from the edge of the table, the power cord winding around the object or fuselage will make the product fall and cause damaged. 13. Do not remove food until the stand mixer is OFF and the cutters stops. 14. Do not attempt to repair the device yourself, since you will be exposed to hazardous live components or other hazards .Repairs should only be carried out in a qualified workshop. 15. No liability is accepted for damage due to improper use or the failure to observe our operating instructions / safety notes.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71UK6BmWa4L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"SaWaUto","source_asin":"B08PKM5VC5","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-674957","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08PKM5VC5","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B08PKM5VC5","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
